{{Wiki_Page | content=
=Introduction to Logic=
There are two key types of logic blocks with an extra section. The first is numeric, numeric logic blocks allow the user to manipulate numerical data, for example plus to input values together. The second is boolean, boolean logic allows for a true or false style of logic, for example opening/closing doors or on/off for lights.

Stormworks has two ways of impliment logic, either directly by placing them on a creation in the workshop, or by using them in a microcontroller. 

=Numeric=
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Add | image=Add.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* adds two numbers
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Subtract | image=Subtract.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* subtracts two numbers
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Multiply | image=Multiply.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* multiplies two numbers
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Divide | image=Divide.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* divides two numbers
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Abs | image=Abs.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* the absolute value of a number
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Clamp | image=Clamp.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* cuts off the input number at the given limits
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Constant Number | image=Constant Number.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Output 1 (Number): the defined value
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Exponent | image=Exponent.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number): the exponent of both inputs
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Greater than | image=Greater Than.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (On/Off)
* Outputs either true or false depending if Input 1 is greater than Input 2 or not.
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Less than | image=Less Than.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (On/Off)
* Outputs either true or false depending if Input 1 is less than Input 2 or not.
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Threshold Gate | image=Threshold Gate.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* The output is "On" if the tested value is in the defined interval
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Modulo | image=Modulo.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* calculate the modulo of two numbers
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Numerical Inverter | image=Numerical Inverter.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* inverts the input number: <code>f(-x)</code>
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Trigonometry | image=Trigonometry.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* can output different functions such as sin, cos, tan
}}





=Boolean (True/False)=
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=And | image=And.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off)
* Input 2 (On/Off)
* Output 1 (On/Off)
* if both inputs are on
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Not | image=Not.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off)
* Output 1 (On/Off)
* inverts the input ("On"->"Off", "Off"->"On")
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Constant On | image=Constant On.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Output 1 (On/Off): always outputs "On"
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=JK Flip Flop | image=JK Flip Flop.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off): Set Flip Flop to "On"
* Input 2 (Number): Set Flip Flop to "Off"
* Output 1 (On/Off): state of the Flip Flop
* Output 2 (On/Off): opposite of the state of the Flip Flop
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Or | image=Or.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off)
* Input 2 (On/Off)
* Output 1 (On/Off): outputs "On" if input 1 or input 2 or both are "On"
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Push to toggle | image=Push To Toggle.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off): change the state ("On"->"Off", "Off"->"On")
* Output 1 (On/Off): state of the toggle
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=SR Latch | image=SR Latch.jpg | content=&nbsp;
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Xor | image=XOR.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off)
* Input 2 (On/Off)
* outputs "On" if only one of the two inputs is "On"
}}



=Composite=


=Functions=
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Function (1 Input) | image=Function 1 Input.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* applies a defined function onto a value
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Function (3 Input) | image=Function 3 Input.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Input 3 (Number)
* Output 1 (Number)
* Same as Function with 1 input but you can use more different inputs in your function
}}

Clamp: Sets both minimum and maximum values for a number. Although it states "clamp x within y and z" without specifying any order, it does require inputs in the order of (input, min, max).


=Other=
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Blinker | image=Blinker.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off): activate blinker
* Output 1 (On/Off)
* outputs "on" in a player defined rate
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Capacitor | image=Capacitor.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off)
* Output 1 (On/Off)
* can delay and/or extend the input signal
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Delay | image=Delay.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off)
* Output 1 (On/Off)
* delays the change of the input signal (it will extend and delay the "On" state)
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Counter | image=Counter.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off): is active
* Output 1 (Number): the current counter value
* after a defined time increases the counter value by 1
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Counter (Ping Pong) | image=Counter Ping Pong.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (On/Off): is active
* Output 1 (Number): the current counter value
* after a defined time increases the counter value by 1 until it reaches its upper limit. Then it will count -1 until it reaches its lower limit ... and again and again
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Memory | image=Memory.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number): the value to write to the memory
* Input 2 (On/Off): write value to memory now
* Input 3 (On/Off): reset memory to defined value (default: 0)
* Output 1 (Number): value in the memory
* can be used to store a value over time
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Numerical Junction | image=Numerical Junction.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (On/Off): use output 2
* Output 1 (Number): outputs value of input 1 (if input 2 = "Off")
* Output 2 (Number): outputs value of input 1 (if input 2 = "On")
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Numerical Switchbox | image=Numerical Switchbox.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number)
* Input 2 (Number)
* Input 3 (On/Off): use input 2
* Output 1 (Number): outputs value of input 1 (if input 3 = "Off") and value of input 2 (if input 3 = "On")
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Up/Down | image=Up Down.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* outputs 1 if "On" and -1 if "Off"
}}




=Microcontroller=
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=[[Wiki/Building/Microcontrollers | Microcontroller]] | image=Microcontroller.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* This holds logic components and is used to organize groups of logic components and save space. It is the only way to read or write composite data.
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=Gyro | image=Gyro.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Can be used to control a helicopter like vehicle
}}
{{Wiki_Component_Description | title=PID Controller | image=PID Controller.jpg | content=&nbsp;
* Input 1 (Number): the target value
* Input 2 (Number): the current measured value
* Input 3 (On/Off): is active
* Output 1 (Number): the value used to control the measured value
* can be used to e.g. control the speed and throttle of a vehicle or engine
}}
















}}
